Falsifies `byte_sink_contract::verification::severity_reads_back_clamped_and_leaves_the_rest`.

The defect: `with_severity` clamps a level past debug to eight, a value `severity` does not read
as a level, so the clamped level reads back as unset.

Expected to fail: the harness's claim that the level reads back as `min(level, 7)`; Kani reports
it failing for any level above 7.

diff --git a/crates/byte_sink_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/byte_sink_contract/src/lib.rs
index 7bf381b61..bb56f9fd7 100644
--- a/crates/byte_sink_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/byte_sink_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -207,7 +207,7 @@ pub const fn severity(w0: u64) -> Option<u8> {
 /// least alarming reading of a level nobody defined). It acts on any first word, but only a bytes
 /// message's bits are read.
 pub const fn with_severity(w0: u64, level: u8) -> u64 {
-    let level = if level > 7 { 7 } else { level };
+    let level = if level > 7 { 8 } else { level };
     (w0 & !(0xff << SEVERITY_SHIFT)) | (((level as u64) + 1) << SEVERITY_SHIFT)
 }
 
